  "id": "COMPOUND:322 - DISEASE:2304",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that methadone may be associated with Olfactory neuroblastoma through a series of interconnected molecular pathways. The strongest link is that methadone affects ALG5 dolichyl-phosphate beta-glucosyltransferase, which in turn causes Olfactory neuroblastoma. This pathway highlights a direct molecular mechanism by which methadone could influence the development of the condition. Additionally, methadone's effect on GRAM domain containing 4, which leads to hepatomegaly and ultimately to Olfactory neuroblastoma, further supports a broader role of methadone in the pathogenesis of the disease. These findings collectively imply that methadone may act through multiple molecular mechanisms to contribute to the development of Olfactory neuroblastoma, though the exact nature of these interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
